<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48662" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tractōrĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		traho. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>for drawing</i> or <i>hoisting</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">genus machinarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr.
					10, 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Substt.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tractō-rĭa</span></b> , ae,
				f. (sc. epistula), <i>a letter of
				invitation</i> or <i>summons</i>, <i><span class="en">Aug. Ep.
				217</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trac-tōrĭae</span></b> ,
			ārum, f. (sc. litterae), <i>an imperial letter containing an order to provide a
				person with necessaries on his journey</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">de tractoriis et stativis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 15, 52</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
